1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
FBX file format

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Now, when using the FBX file format,

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
add or remove multiple virtual models at the same time.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Through this function,

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
you can add other objects or virtual models

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
when you keep the object in the current scene.

7
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Go to the menu,

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,000
File, Add or Add,

9
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,000
select the FBX format,

10
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,000
select the file you need to import,

11
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,000
and select Open.

12
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,000
In the FBX dialogue box,

13
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
change the load type to Add.

14
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,000
You can choose Avatar or Trim as the target type.

15
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Now, when you import or add FBX files,

16
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
it will have the same settings as importing OPJ files.

17
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Select a copy,

18
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
then click on the water glue tool on the top right of the location ball

19
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,000
and stick it on the costume.

20
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Repeat the process,

21
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,000
import and copy multiple FBX files

22
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,000
and continue other operations.

23
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Using the FBX file format,

24
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:52,000
import or remove multiple virtual models

25
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
will help you better complete the multi-role scene production,

26
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
instead of only using the content of one role.

27
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Select the FBX file you want to import.

28
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,000
In the FBX dialogue box,

29
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:04,000
set the load type to Add,

30
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,000
and the target type to virtual model.

31
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,000
For the human-type virtual model,

32
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,000
click on Automated Automated Portrait,

33
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,000
and it will automatically create a portrait in the import process.

34
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,000
In the object bar,

35
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,000
you can choose the relevant content of the import file,

36
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,000
such as joint animation.

37
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Now you can set the axis rotation

38
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,000
or enter the moving value

39
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,000
to adjust the virtual model to the right position.

40
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Here I will set the moving value of the two-meter Z axis.

41
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,000
When you enter the moving value,

42
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,000
when an object is placed below the ground,

43
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:33,000
you can click to align the ground.

44
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
They will automatically be placed above the ground after being imported.

45
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Click to move the costume to the starting point of the action.

46
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,000
The costume will automatically move to the virtual model near the starting point.

47
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Click to confirm and click to import the file.

48
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Open the animation editor.

49
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Let's preview the animation.

50
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:54,000
You can import the costume corresponding to the second virtual model,

51
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,000
set the same moving value,

52
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,000
and let them match.

53
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Open the simulation,

54
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,000
wear the costume,

55
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,000
and start recording the animation.

56
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
When exporting FBX files,

57
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
you can also export all virtual models,

58
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,000
or select an independent virtual model to export.

